Root cause of 98% root spans: daemon and relay use BasicTracerProvider without registering a ContextManager. context.active() always returns ROOT_CONTEXT → every span is a root.

Fix (3 lines):
```typescript
import { AsyncLocalStorageContextManager } from '@opentelemetry/context-async-hooks';
const ctxManager = new AsyncLocalStorageContextManager();
ctxManager.enable();
context.setGlobalContextManager(ctxManager);
```

Add to: daemon initTracing() + relay initTracing().
bun add @opentelemetry/context-async-hooks
Also fix relay FileSpanExporter parentSpanId access.

Instantly fixes all 278 existing withSpan calls — they'll chain into proper trace trees.

Add first-class subagent events instead of repurposing task.started/tool.progress/task.completed.

New events:
- subagent.spawned: { agentId, parentTurnId, prompt, model, description }
- subagent.tool_use: { agentId, toolName, summary }  
- subagent.output: { agentId, delta, streamKind }
- subagent.completed: { agentId, status, result, cost, tokens }

Both Claude Code and Codex support subagents. Adapter maps:
- Claude: system.task_started → subagent.spawned, system.task_progress → subagent.tool_use, system.task_notification → subagent.completed
- Codex: similar mapping from their agent events

Benefits: natural grouping in dashboard, cost attribution, nesting (sub-subagent via parentAgentId), unified across providers.

Depends on: orka-c2id (current task.started grouping) as stepping stone.

Implement Noise NK handshake and encrypted transport per spec §2.4-2.5.

Handshake (§2.4):
- Client sends noise_1: { t: 'noise_1', msg: base64url(WriteMessage()) }
- Node sends noise_2: { t: 'noise_2', msg: base64url(WriteMessage()) }
- Both call Split() → send/receive CipherState
- session_id = GetHandshakeHash()

Encrypted frames (§2.5):
- Wire: { t: 'data', ct: base64url(Noise transport ciphertext) }
- Plaintext inside ct: { v: 1, kind: 'rpc', rpc: { jsonrpc: '2.0', ... } }
- Nonce NOT transmitted on wire (ordered WebSocket, Noise manages internally)

Session binding:
- session_id stored for future client auth channel binding

Files: packages/core/src/transport/noise-transport.ts (new)

Define all pairing message types as zod schemas per spec §1.5.

Messages:
- pair_client_hello: { t, v, pair_suites[], client_instance_id, features[] }
- pair_server_hello: { t, v, pair_suite, enroll_id, expires_in_sec, features[] }
- pair_init: { t, pA (base64url SPAKE2 public value) }
- pair_resp: { t, pB (base64url SPAKE2 public value) }
- pair_confirm1: { t, mac (base64url) }
- pair_confirm2: { t, mac (base64url) }
- pair_bootstrap: { t, ct (base64url encrypted payload) }
- pair_done: { t }
- pair_error: { t, code: expired|not_found|attempts_exhausted|bad_version|bad_suite|protocol_error }

Also:
- pair_context = CanonicalJSON(client_hello) || CanonicalJSON(server_hello)
- pair_aad = 'orka-pair/v1' || relay_origin || pair_context

Bootstrap plaintext schema:
- { node_id, node_name, noise_suite, noise_static_pubkey, noise_key_id, node_paths[], rpc[] }

