Currently frontends (dashboard, CLI) duplicate state machine logic to decide which buttons to show. This causes bugs (e.g. can't resume cancelled sessions because frontend doesn't know it's allowed).

Fix: daemon returns allowedActions[] with every session response. Frontend just renders what's allowed.

```typescript
interface SessionResponse {
  // ...existing fields...
  allowedActions: SessionAction[];
}
type SessionAction = 'sendTurn' | 'stop' | 'resume' | 'cancel' | 'merge' | 'retry' | 'archive' | 'delete';
```

Daemon computes allowedActions based on status + runtime state (live handle, worktree exists, etc.). Single source of truth — no duplicated logic in frontends.

Dashboard: show/hide buttons based on allowedActions. Input enabled only if sendTurn in allowedActions.
CLI: same logic for interactive commands.

After creating a git worktree for an agent session, the worktree has no node_modules. Agents then waste time and tokens trying to install dependencies (often failing due to sandbox).

Fix: in orchestrator.ts, after worktreeCreate(), symlink node_modules from the main repo:
```typescript
import { symlinkSync } from 'node:fs';
// After worktreeCreate:
symlinkSync(join(projectPath, 'node_modules'), join(workingDir, 'node_modules'));
```

This gives agents immediate access to all workspace dependencies without needing bun install.

