## What
Add Tailwind CSS custom utilities in index.css for mobile-specific needs: safe-area padding classes and a mobile bottom bar height offset.

## Files
- \`packages/dashboard/src/index.css\`

## Details
- This project uses Tailwind v4 (CSS-based config via \`@import \"tailwindcss\"\`).
- Add custom utility classes via \`@utility\` directives (Tailwind v4 syntax):

\`\`\`css
@utility pb-safe {
  padding-bottom: env(safe-area-inset-bottom);
}

@utility pt-safe {
  padding-top: env(safe-area-inset-top);
}

@utility pb-tabbar {
  padding-bottom: calc(4rem + env(safe-area-inset-bottom));
}
\`\`\`

- \`pb-tabbar\` accounts for the ~64px bottom tab bar plus the safe area, used on the main content area to prevent content from being hidden behind the fixed bottom nav.
- These utilities make it easy to apply safe-area offsets throughout the mobile layout.
- Alternatively, if Tailwind v4 supports \`env()\` in arbitrary values (e.g., \`pb-[env(safe-area-inset-bottom)]\`), document that approach. But explicit utility classes are cleaner.

## Acceptance
- \`pb-safe\`, \`pt-safe\`, and \`pb-tabbar\` utility classes are available.
- They apply the correct safe-area inset padding.
- They compose with other Tailwind classes normally.
